{title: Narrow Gate}
{subtitle: Matthew 7:13–14}
{key: Gm}
{tempo: 144}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Gm] | [Gm] | [Gm] | [Gm] |
| [Gm] | [Eb7] | [Eb7] | [Gm] |
| [Gm] | [Gm] | [Gm] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Wide is the gate and broad is the road
It leads to destruction, many go through
The [Cm7]path is easy to follow
But the [Eb7]end brings only [D7]loss
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Gm]Enter through the narrow gate
Where the road is hard and steep
[Ebmaj7]Few find the [D7]way to [Gm]life
[Ebmaj7]Keep your watch and [D7]stay a[Gm]lert
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Beware of false prophets near
Sheep's clothing hides the wolf
Look at the fruit they bear
To know if they are true
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Ebmaj7]Enter through the [D7]narrow gate
Where the [Gm]road is hard and steep
[Ebmaj7]Few find the [D7]way to [Gm]life
[Ebmaj7]Keep your watch and [D7]stay a[Gm]lert
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Ebmaj7]Good trees bring [D7]good fruit to [Gm]see
[Ebmaj7]Rotten [D7]trees give [Gm]bad fruit
[Ebmaj7]Recog[D7]nize them by their [Gm]ways
[Ebmaj7]Do not be de[D7]ceived by [Gm]looks
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[D7]The narrow road [Ebmaj7]leads to life
Few find it, but [D7]it [Gm]waits
[Ebmaj7]Enter through the [D7]narrow [Gm]gate
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
